PROPORTIONAL-ODDS ASSUMPTION NOTE
======================================================================
Outcome levels 3 and 4 are sparse (level 3: n=11, level 4: n=7).
The proportional-odds (common-OR) model assumes the BCG, priorMH and their
interaction shift all cumulative severity thresholds by the same log-odds amount.
With only 11 observations at level 3 and 7 at level 4, the top-threshold
estimates (and hence the interaction OR) are imprecise; see the wide CI.
A non-proportional-odds (partial-proportional) model could relax this but
is under-powered at n=153 with a 4-way interaction.

